{title: 032 - When in Our Music God is Glorified}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #032 • ENGELBERG • 9.11.10.3}
{lyricist: Fred Pratt Green}
{composer: Charles V. Stanford}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 32}
{meta: tune ENGELBERG}
{meta: meter 9.11.10.3}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]When [G]in [Bm]our [Am]music [Em]God [F#dim]is [G]glorified,
[D]And adoration [F#dim]leaves [Bm]no [Am]room [Em]for [D]pride,
[D/A]It [Bm]is as [D]though [G]the [Am]whole [Bm]creation cried:
[Bm]Alleluia!

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]How [G]oft, [Bm]in [Am]making [Em]music, [G]we [Em]have [D]found
[D]A new [D7]dimension [G]in [Bm]the [Am]world [Em]of [D]sound,
[Bm]As worship moved us to a more [Am]profound
[Bm]Alleluia! [C]Alleluia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]And [G]did [Bm]not [Am]Jesus [Em]sing [F#dim]a [G]psalm [Em]that [D]night
[D]When utmost [Bm]evil [G]strove [Bm]against [Em]the [D]light?
[Bm]Then let us sing for whom He won [Am]the fight:
[Bm]Alleluia! [C]Alleluia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Let every [Am]instrument [F#dim]be [G]used [Em]for [D]praise;
[D]Let all [D7]rejoice [F#dim]who [G]have [Bm]a [Am]voice [Em]to [D]raise;
[Bm]And may God give us faith to sing [Am]always:
[Bm]Alleluia! [C]Alleluia!
{end_of_verse}
